---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import ToolPage from '../../components/ToolPage.astro';
import { buildGameFacts } from '../../lib/game-catalog';

const games = (await getCollection('games')).filter((game) => !game.data.draft);
const facts = buildGameFacts(games).map((fact) => ({
  id: fact.slug,
  title: fact.title,
  genre: fact.genre,
  sessionLabel: fact.sessionLabel,
  sessionMin: fact.sessionMin,
  sessionMax: fact.sessionMax,
  players: fact.players,
  inputs: fact.inputs,
}));

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Are session labels promises?',
    a: 'No. They are estimated ranges from typical play in the catalog. A session planner can suggest a count; it cannot promise how long any player will take.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How is the run estimate calculated?',
    a: 'It rounds the session midpoint to a whole minute, divides your available minutes by that value, rounds down, and displays at least one run. A displayed run is not a guarantee it will fit; the planner does not exclude games based on your time budget.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does it save my answers?',
    a: 'No. Everything stays in page memory and disappears on reload. The tool writes no storage at all.',
  },
];
---

<ToolPage
  title="Session planner"
  eyebrow="Minutes × players × input"
  description="Turn a free minute count into a shortlist of games and an estimated number of runs, then open them directly. Player and input filters apply on top."
  path="/tools/session-planner/"
  category="Play"
  bottomLine="The planner takes the minutes you have, plus players and input, and lists matching NoCharge games with an estimated runs-per-session. It is an estimate from catalog session labels, not a timer and not a promise."
  faqs={faqs}
  embedCode={`<iframe src="https://nocharge.net/tools/session-planner/" width="400" height="620" title="NoCharge session planner"></iframe>`}
  nextActions={[
    { href: '/arcade/', label: 'Open the Arcade', note: 'The same catalog, with chips and sort controls.' },
    { href: '/tools/game-finder/', label: 'Game Finder quiz', note: 'A different way to filter by what fits today.' },
    { href: '/learn/untimed-play/', label: 'Untimed play explainer', note: 'Why “untimed” is not the same as “short”.' },
  ]}
>
  <section class="panel planner-controls" aria-labelledby="planner-heading">
    <div>
      <p class="section-kicker">Plan a break</p>
      <h2 id="planner-heading">How long do you have?</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="planner-grid">
      <label>Minutes available
        <input type="number" min="1" max="240" value="10" data-planner-min aria-label="Minutes available" />
      </label>
      <label>Players
        <select data-planner-players aria-label="Players">
          <option value="any">Any</option>
          <option value="solo">Solo</option>
          <option value="pass-and-play">Pass &amp; Play</option>
        </select>
      </label>
      <label>Input
        <select data-planner-input aria-label="Input">
          <option value="any">Any</option>
          <option value="keyboard">Keyboard</option>
          <option value="pointer">Pointer</option>
          <option value="touch">Touch</option>
        </select>
      </label>
    </div>
    <div id="planner-results" class="planner-results" data-games={JSON.stringify(facts)} aria-live="polite"></div>
  </section>
  <Fragment slot="how">
    <p>The planner first filters by players and supported input. It sorts matching games by the upper end of their session range, then by title, and displays at most 12 cards. Minutes change the run estimate; they do not remove a game from the list.</p>
    <h3>Worked example</h3>
    <p>Memory Match is labeled 2–5 minutes. Its midpoint is (2 + 5) ÷ 2 = 3.5, rounded to 4 minutes. With 10 minutes available, the estimate is floor(10 ÷ 4) = 2 runs. The remaining 2 minutes are not allocated to setup, pauses, or switching games.</p>
    <p>In general, the displayed count is the available minutes divided by the rounded midpoint, rounded down, with a minimum of one. Inputs are limited to 1–240 minutes. A one-minute budget can therefore still display one run of a longer game; check the session label alongside the count.</p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="limits">
    <ul>
      <li>This is an estimate, not a timer, reservation, or proof that the displayed runs fit your break.</li>
      <li>The calculation does not use your personal completion history or allow time for reading rules and taking turns.</li>
      <li>Only the first 12 sorted matches are displayed even when the summary counts more candidates.</li>
      <li>A supported-input flag does not necessarily mean every action is possible with that input alone. Use Game Finder's keyboard-complete filter for that stricter requirement.</li>
      <li>Changing these controls does not save a schedule, start a reminder, or modify any game.</li>
    </ul>
  </Fragment>
</ToolPage>

<script>
  interface Fact { id: string; title: string; genre: string; sessionLabel: string; sessionMin: number; sessionMax: number; players: 'solo' | 'pass-and-play'; inputs: string[]; }
  const minutes = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-planner-min]');
  const players = document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-planner-players]');
  const input = document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-planner-input]');
  const results = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#planner-results');
  if (minutes && players && input && results) {
    const games = JSON.parse(results.dataset.games ?? '[]') as Fact[];
    const render = () => {
      const total = Math.max(1, Math.min(240, Number(minutes.value) || 10));
      const playerValue = players.value;
      const inputValue = input.value;
      const matched = games.filter((game) => {
        if (playerValue !== 'any' && game.players !== playerValue) return false;
        if (inputValue !== 'any' && !game.inputs.includes(inputValue)) return false;
        return true;
      }).sort((a, b) => a.sessionMax - b.sessionMax || a.title.localeCompare(b.title));
      results.replaceChildren();
      if (matched.length === 0) {
        results.textContent = 'No game matches both filters. Broaden one to see results — nothing was ignored.';
        return;
      }
      const summary = document.createElement('p');
      summary.textContent = `${total} min · ${playerValue === 'any' ? 'any players' : playerValue === 'solo' ? 'solo' : 'two players'} · ${inputValue === 'any' ? 'any input' : inputValue} — ${matched.length} candidate game${matched.length === 1 ? '' : 's'}.`;
      results.append(summary);
      for (const game of matched.slice(0, 12)) {
        const card = document.createElement('article');
        card.className = 'panel planner-card';
        const heading = document.createElement('h3');
        const link = document.createElement('a');
        link.href = `/games/${game.id}/`;
        link.textContent = game.title;
        heading.append(link);
        const midpoint = Math.round((game.sessionMin + game.sessionMax) / 2);
        const approximate = Math.max(1, Math.floor(total / Math.max(1, midpoint)));
        const meta = document.createElement('p');
        meta.textContent = `${game.genre} · ${game.sessionLabel} · about ${approximate} run${approximate === 1 ? '' : 's'} in ${total} min`;
        const actions = document.createElement('p');
        const play = document.createElement('a');
        play.href = `/games/${game.id}/`;
        play.textContent = 'Play';
        const guide = document.createElement('a');
        guide.href = `/guides/${game.id}/`;
        guide.textContent = 'Guide';
        const sep = document.createTextNode(' · ');
        actions.append(play, sep, guide);
        card.append(heading, meta, actions);
        results.append(card);
      }
    };
    for (const control of [minutes, players, input]) control.addEventListener('change', render);
    minutes.addEventListener('input', render);
    render();
  }
</script>

<style is:global>
  .planner-controls {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 1.25rem;
  }

  .planner-controls > div:first-child {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.3rem;
  }

  .planner-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.8rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(10rem, 100%), 1fr));
  }

  .planner-grid label {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.35rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .planner-grid input,
  .planner-grid select {
    min-height: 44px;
    padding: 0.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    background: var(--panel-2);
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .planner-results {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.7rem;
  }

  .planner-results > p:first-child {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  .planner-card {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.3rem;
    padding: 0.9rem;
  }

  .planner-card h3 a {
    color: var(--accent-strong);
  }

  .planner-card p {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.84rem;
  }

  .planner-card p:last-child a {
    color: var(--accent-strong);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
</style>
